# Valgrind suppressions for luaext's best-effort CI leg
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml, job "best-effort" / "valgrind").
#
# Empty because the valgrind leg has needed no suppression against the
# current code. If a real false positive appears (PHP's own persistent
# allocations, OS-level one-time initialization, intentional leaks in Zend
# startup), add it here with a comment explaining why the finding is
# expected and safe, not just what it is. Never add a suppression to make
# a genuine leak in luaext's own code disappear.
#
# Format reference: https://valgrind.org/docs/manual/manual-core.html#manual-core.suppress
#
# Example shape (commented out — nothing suppressed yet):
#
# {
#   example_suppression_name
#   Memcheck:Leak
#   match-leak-kinds: reachable
#   ...
#   fun:example_function_name
# }
